    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d609">

                <pb facs="0737" n="677" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg677"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Gough to Mr.
                            Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Newport, R.
                                I.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-10-10"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 10,
                    1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my note of the 28th
                    ultimo, in which I stated that Rear-Admiral Stephenson would be obliged if
                    arrangements could be made for the necessary witnesses being directed to attend
                    at Victoria to give evidence in the case of the seizure of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Shelby</hi>, and to your reply of the 3d instant, I have
                    now the honor to inform you that I am in receipt of a telegram from Rear-Admiral
                    Stephenson on the subject.</p>
                <p>Admiral Stephenson is anxious to secure the presence at Victoria of the
                    commanders of the U. S. ships <hi rendition="#italic">Corwin</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Rush</hi>, and other officers who can give evidence
                    regarding the seizure of the sealing schooners <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Shelby</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Beatrice</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">E. B. Marvin.</hi></p>
                <p>In the case of the commander and officers of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Corwin</hi>, Admiral Stephenson telegraphs that their immediate presence is
                    desired, whereas in the case of the officers of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Rush</hi>, their testimony as witnesses will not be necessary for a period
                    of from two to three weeks.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gough</hi></signed>.<lb/>(For
                        <signed>Sir Julian Pauncefote</signed>.)</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
